# ============================================================
# flow/keepout_blocks_partner_reach.buda
#
# A trunk placed where its PARTNER cannot reach it.  THIS IS AN
# OPEN DEFECT.  Sibling of flow/antenna_culled_partner.buda —
# same geometry, same cull, DIFFERENT cause:
#
#   antenna_culled_partner  keepout declared AFTER run_planner,
#                           so the pass ORDER strands metal
#   this vehicle            keepout declared UP FRONT, and the
#                           PLACER still walks into it
#
# NUTS places each segment against keepouts ON ITS OWN LAYER.
# The trunk here is H on M4; the keepout is on M5.  So the trunk
# sees no obstacle, takes the middle of its window, and the V
# stub that has to climb from it into `rcv` is left with no
# legal position at all.
#
# What the engine itself reports about that window:
#
#   seg1  H M4  along[190,710] perp=525  slide=[220..580]=360
#         pull=none(0)  opt=[200..600]  anchors=2/2
#
# `pull=none(0)` and a flat optimum spanning the whole window:
# moving the trunk trades one V stub's length for the other's,
# so EVERY position costs the same wirelength.  The placer takes
# the centre — exactly 400 — and 400 is inside the keepout's
# y-band (380..450).  Only perp >= 450 keeps the partner clear,
# so about a third of the window is legal and the default lands
# in the other two thirds.  The candidate's own nominal (525) is
# legal; the placer moves off it for no gain.
#
# MEASURED (this vehicle, three ways):
#
#   as written, no healer      4 bits unplaced, 4 violations
#   + ripup_reroute            clean, detailed WL 4297
#   trunk slid to [460,580]    clean, detailed WL 3715
#
# The healer rescues it in one move — by RE-PINNING to a detour
# topology (V at perp=20, around the outside), not by nudging
# the trunk.  That is +15.7% detailed WL to buy back what a
# 60-unit slide inside a WL-FLAT window would have given free.
#
# The engine is not silent.  run_nuts says:
#
#   junction infeasible: bundle 1 seg 0 cannot reach seg 1
#   WARNING: 1 segment(s) placed ON a keepout (window exhausted)
#
# So the information exists at placement time.  What is missing
# is using it: nothing consults a partner's keepouts when
# choosing among positions the segment's own layer allows.
#
# The vehicle ends DIRTY on purpose (4 unplaced bits): that IS
# the defect.  Do not add it to the QoR corpus.
#
# Run:  bin/buda flow/keepout_blocks_partner_reach.buda --no-viz
# ============================================================

def_layer 4 M4 H TOP 33.33
def_layer 5 M5 V TOP 33.33
def_track_pattern 4 0  POWER 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4  GROUND 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4
def_track_pattern 5 0  POWER 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4  GROUND 2 1  (SIGNAL 1 0.5)x4

# Up front, unlike the culled-partner twin: the planner sees it.
add_keepout 600 380 900 450 5
corner_margin dx 10 dy 10

add_block drv  100 100  200 200
add_block rcv  700 600  800 700
add_bus b[4] drv.tx rcv.rx

run_bundler strict
generate_topologies

# Candidate 4 is Z_VHV@y525@x190 — V up from drv, H across, V
# into rcv.  Pinned so the vehicle shows ONE shape; the pin is by
# index, so a change to candidate ORDER moves it.
select_topology 1 4

run_planner
run_nuts
run_detailed_nuts
dump_topologies --conn
check_design dnuts
report_wirelength
